# Generated by chartgen from this template and the executable Redfish registry.
plugin_name: go.d.plugin
modules:
  - meta:
      id: collector-go.d.plugin-redfish
      plugin_name: go.d.plugin
      module_name: redfish
      monitored_instance:
        name: Redfish
        link: https://www.dmtf.org/standards/redfish
        icon_filename: hardware.svg
        categories:
          - data-collection.hardware-and-sensors
      keywords:
        - redfish
        - bmc
        - out-of-band
        - hardware
        - server
        - idrac
        - ilo
      related_resources:
        integrations:
          list:
            - plugin_name: go.d.plugin
              module_name: redfish_logs
      info_provided_to_referring_integrations:
        description: ""
    overview:
      data_collection:
        metrics_description: |
          Monitor standard DMTF Redfish resources exposed by a baseboard management controller (BMC).

          The collector covers endpoint health, systems, chassis, managers, processors, memory, storage, drives, volumes,
          network adapters and ports, PCIe, power, cooling, environmental sensors, batteries, leak detection, firmware,
          assemblies, and LogService state. It publishes:

          - per-component metrics and state charts;
          - complete one-level rollups with population/completeness, min/average/max, fixed histograms, and state counts;
          - deterministic ComputerSystem virtual nodes when `node_mode: system_vnodes` is selected;
          - current hardware inventory through `redfish:inventory`;
          - retained LogService records through `redfish:logs` when a referenced `redfish_logs` backend is ready.
        method_description: |
          The collector authenticates to the Redfish ServiceRoot over HTTP or HTTPS, traverses only its closed standard-resource
          registry, and follows same-origin links. It prefers session authentication in `auto` mode and falls back to HTTP Basic
          authentication when the endpoint does not support a usable session. Requests are bounded by the configured timeout,
          retry count, and concurrency.

          Collection is best-effort: one unreadable resource does not stop independently reachable resources. Missing current
          values produce gaps rather than zeroes. Complete membership scans obsolete removed components; partial scans retain
          prior membership evidence without replaying stale readings.
      supported_platforms:
        include: []
        exclude: []
      multi_instance: true
      additional_permissions:
        description: |
          A read-only Redfish account is normally required. No local elevated privileges are needed. Log storage requires the
          Netdata log directory to be writable by the Agent through a configured `redfish_logs` job.
      default_behavior:
        auto_detection:
          description: |
            No endpoint is auto-detected by the collector itself. Configure static jobs, DynCfg jobs, or enable the independent
            Redfish Service Discovery pipeline under `go.d/sd/redfish.conf`.
        limits:
          description: |
            Detailed component charts are admitted atomically per logical owner and component family. The default cap is 100
            components per family; exceeding it suppresses that whole detail group while preserving inventory and complete
            one-level rollups. Set `charts.max_detailed_components_per_family: 0` for no configurable cap.

            LogService admission is atomic across the selected services and defaults to 256 services. Protocol response bounds,
            closed traversal registries, and request concurrency protect the Agent from malformed or hostile payloads.
        performance_impact:
          description: |
            The default interval is 60 seconds. BMCs are often slow and may serialize requests internally. The collector starts
            conservatively with three concurrent requests and uses the configured ceiling unless the ServiceRoot explicitly
            prohibits multiple HTTP requests, in which case it uses one. It does not probe or automatically change the job's
            cadence. The complete endpoint walk is also bounded by the configured `update_every`; when it cannot finish, the
            collector publishes independently completed data as partial and rotates unfinished member work across later cycles.
            Use a larger `update_every`, narrower `collect` pattern, or lower concurrency if the BMC becomes overloaded.
    setup:
      prerequisites:
        list:
          - title: Enable and authorize Redfish
            description: |
              Enable the BMC's Redfish service and create a least-privilege monitoring account that can read the desired systems,
              chassis, managers, sensors, storage, and LogService entries.
          - title: Establish network and TLS trust
            description: |
              Ensure the Netdata Agent can reach the BMC. Prefer HTTPS with a trusted BMC certificate or configure `tls_ca`.
              `tls_skip_verify` is available for legacy/self-signed deployments but permits machine-in-the-middle attacks.
          - title: Configure a log backend if logs are required
            description: |
              Redfish metrics do not require log storage. To ingest LogService entries, configure and enable a `redfish_logs` job.
              Omitted endpoint routing selects the backend job named `default`; an explicit missing backend never falls back.
      configuration:
        file:
          name: go.d/redfish.conf
        options:
          description: |
            The following options apply per Redfish endpoint job. Credentials and private-key fields support Netdata secret
            references such as `${env:VARIABLE}` and `${file:/path}`.
          folding:
            title: Config options
            enabled: true
          list:
            - name: update_every
              group: Collection
              description: Endpoint metric and LogService polling interval in seconds.
              default_value: 60
              required: false
            - name: autodetection_retry
              group: Collection
              description: Failed initial-check retry interval in seconds. Zero disables retries.
              default_value: 0
              required: false
            - name: url
              group: Target
              description: Redfish origin or ServiceRoot URL. HTTP and HTTPS are supported.
              default_value: ""
              required: true
            - name: node_mode
              group: Virtual Node
              description: "`local` publishes on the collecting node; `system_vnodes` creates deterministic ComputerSystem HostScopes."
              default_value: ""
              required: true
            - name: vnode
              group: Virtual Node
              description: Associates local-mode output with an existing configured virtual node.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: system_uri
              group: Target
              description: Optional exact same-origin ComputerSystem URI filter; empty selects every system.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: auth_method
              group: Authentication
              description: Authentication mode (`auto`, `session`, `basic`, or `none`). Auto prefers session and falls back to Basic.
              default_value: auto
              required: false
            - name: username
              group: Authentication
              description: "Redfish username. Required except with `auth_method: none`."
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: password
              group: Authentication
              description: Redfish password. Use a Netdata secret reference.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: timeout
              group: HTTP
              description: Per-request timeout.
              default_value: 15
              required: false
            - name: retries
              group: HTTP
              description: Additional attempts for eligible transient GET failures.
              default_value: 2
              required: false
            - name: max_concurrent_requests
              group: HTTP
              description: Maximum requests in flight against this endpoint.
              default_value: 3
              required: false
            - name: proxy_url
              group: HTTP
              description: Explicit HTTP/HTTPS proxy URL. Empty uses the process environment proxy policy.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: tls_ca
              group: TLS
              description: CA certificate bundle used to verify the Redfish HTTPS endpoint.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: tls_cert
              group: TLS
              description: Optional client certificate. Must be configured together with `tls_key`.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: tls_key
              group: TLS
              description: Optional client private key. Use a Netdata secret reference.
              default_value: ""
              required: false
            - name: tls_skip_verify
              group: TLS
              description: Disable HTTPS certificate verification. Use only when secure trust configuration is not possible.
              default_value: false
              required: false
            - name: collect
              group: Collection
              description: Simple-pattern selector over base, compute, memory, thermal, power, storage, network, pcie, sensors, and firmware. Base is always collected.
              default_value: "*"
              required: false
            - name: charts.aggregates
              group: Cardinality
              description: Enable complete one-level aggregate charts.
              default_value: true
              required: false
            - name: charts.details
              group: Cardinality
              description: Enable per-component detail charts.
              default_value: true
              required: false
            - name: charts.max_detailed_components_per_family
              group: Cardinality
              description: Atomic detail admission cap per logical owner and component family. Zero means unlimited.
              default_value: 100
              required: false
            - name: alarms.evaluate_thresholds
              group: Alerts
              description: Evaluate usable source warning/critical thresholds when the BMC reading state is absent or clear; an abnormal BMC state remains authoritative.
              default_value: true
              required: false
            - name: host_scope_overrides
              group: Virtual Node
              description: "Optional ComputerSystem URI to GUID/hostname overrides for deterministic generated HostScopes; used only with `node_mode: system_vnodes`."
              default_value: "[]"
              required: false
            - name: logs.enabled
              group: Logs
              description: Poll eligible LogServices only while the selected backend is ready.
              default_value: true
              required: false
            - name: logs.backend
              group: Logs
              description: Exact `redfish_logs` job name. Omit to select `default`; an explicit unavailable name never falls back.
              default_value: default
              required: false
            - name: logs.service_selector
              group: Logs
              description: Simple-pattern selector matched against discovered LogService identities.
              default_value: "*"
              required: false
            - name: logs.max_services
              group: Logs
              description: Maximum selected LogServices admitted as one atomic set.
              default_value: 256
              required: false
            - name: logs.full_reconciliation_every
              group: Logs
              description: Interval between complete LogEntry source reconciliations. Zero disables periodic reconciliation.
              default_value: 30m
              required: false
            - name: logs.cursor.orphan_retention
              group: Logs
              description: How long inactive LogService cursor records are retained. Zero retains them indefinitely.
              default_value: 720h
              required: false
        examples:
          folding:
            title: Config
            enabled: true
          list:
            - name: Central out-of-band monitoring with vnodes
              description: Create one deterministic Netdata vnode for each ComputerSystem exposed by the BMC.
              config: |
                jobs:
                  - name: bmc
                    url: https://192.0.2.1/redfish/v1/
                    node_mode: system_vnodes
                    username: monitoring
                    password: ${file:/etc/netdata/redfish-password}
                    tls_ca: /etc/netdata/redfish-ca.pem
            - name: In-band collection without duplicate nodes
              description: Publish the local server's BMC metrics on the existing Netdata node.
              config: |
                jobs:
                  - name: local-bmc
                    url: https://192.0.2.1/redfish/v1/
                    node_mode: local
                    system_uri: /redfish/v1/Systems/1
                    username: monitoring
                    password: ${file:/etc/netdata/redfish-password}
    troubleshooting:
      problems:
        list:
          - name: The endpoint check fails
            description: |
              Verify the ServiceRoot URL, reachability, account permissions, authentication mode, proxy policy, and TLS trust.
              `tls_skip_verify: true` can diagnose certificate problems but is not a secure permanent fix.
          - name: Collection takes close to or longer than the interval
            description: |
              BMCs can be slow and frequently serialize work. Lower `max_concurrent_requests`, increase `timeout` only when
              responses genuinely need it, increase `update_every`, or narrow `collect`.
          - name: Detailed charts are absent but aggregates exist
            description: |
              The component-family population exceeded `charts.max_detailed_components_per_family`, or `charts.details` is false.
              The gate is atomic: the collector never selects an arbitrary subset that would break continuity.
          - name: Redfish logs are unavailable
            description: |
              Ensure the selected `redfish_logs` job exists, is enabled, and is ready. Omitted routing selects `default`.
              An explicitly configured missing or disabled backend does not fall back.
          - name: The same endpoint appears through more than one collector owner
            description: |
              Deterministic Redfish vnode GUIDs preserve identity but do not elect one collector. Differently named jobs and
              collectors on different Agents can still poll and publish the same endpoint concurrently, which duplicates metrics
              and creates a vnode identity conflict. Assign one active owner for each endpoint when using `system_vnodes`, or use
              deliberate `local` placement when the endpoint data should stay on separate collector nodes.
          - name: A standard resource is missing or incomplete
            description: |
              Initial compatibility evidence covers DMTF 2026.1 public schema types and embedded redundancy/leak-detection
              shapes, sanitized Dell- and HPE-derived payload shapes, a modern standalone Sensor shape, and synthetic protocol
              faults. Unauthenticated ServiceRoot reachability was exercised on three lab BMCs from Gigabyte and ASRock Rack;
              their models and firmware were not recorded, and no authenticated resource walk was exercised. Consequently, no
              vendor/model/firmware combination is claimed as live-validated, and the evidence does not prove authenticated
              sessions, throttling, or full-cycle timing. No Redfish emulator was run for this qualification. Start new hardware
              qualification with a Netdata nightly build, inspect partial-collection and compatibility diagnostics, and report
              the affected vendor, model, firmware, and sanitized payload shape when a standard resource is missing.
    alerts:
{{GENERATED_ALERTS}}
    functions:
      description: Live views backed by the latest collector snapshots and retained Redfish LogService journals.
      list:
        - id: inventory
          name: Redfish Inventory
          description: |
            Returns the complete current standard inventory slice selected by Redfish job, host, and resource kind. Rows include
            resource identity, ownership, acquisition state, status, source provenance, readings, thresholds, and applicable
            type-specific inventory fields. The Function does not filter or page rows after the required source slice is selected.
          parameters:
            - id: __job
              name: Redfish Job
              description: Select exactly one active Redfish endpoint job.
              type: select
              required: true
              default: ""
              options: []
            - id: host
              name: Host
              description: Select exactly one ComputerSystem or service scope exposed by the selected job.
              type: select
              required: true
              default: ""
              options: []
            - id: resource_kind
              name: Resource Kind
              description: Select exactly one standard Redfish resource kind.
              type: select
              required: true
              default: ""
              options: []
          returns:
            description: Current resource and normalized-reading rows for the exact selected source slice.
            columns:
              - name: resource_kind
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Normalized Redfish resource kind.
              - name: name
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Current source display name.
              - name: resource_uri
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Canonical same-origin Redfish resource URI.
              - name: acquisition_state
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Current readable, unreadable, or unknown acquisition state.
              - name: health
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Current normalized Redfish Health value when present.
              - name: logical_owner_name
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Proven logical ComputerSystem owner when one exists.
              - name: reading_value
                type: float
                unit: ""
                description: Normalized numeric reading for reading rows.
          performance: |
            Uses the latest immutable in-memory snapshots and performs no Redfish requests. A selected source slice may contain
            thousands of rows; the Function returns it as one table because Netdata table Functions do not paginate.
          security: |
            Exposes hardware identifiers, inventory, locations, firmware, source properties, and readings. It never exposes
            Redfish passwords, tokens, session locations, cookies, client keys, or proxy authorization headers.
          availability: Available after at least one active endpoint job publishes an inventory snapshot.
        - id: logs
          name: Redfish Logs
          description: |
            Queries retained Redfish LogService entries across one or more ready named log backends, with the standard Netdata
            logs facets, histogram, full-text search, time range, and source selectors.
          parameters:
            - id: __logs_sources
              name: Redfish Log Backends
              description: Select one or more ready Redfish log backends, or all.
              type: multiselect
              required: false
              default: all
              options: []
          returns:
            description: Historical structured Redfish LogEntry rows returned by the Netdata journal SDK.
            columns:
              - name: MESSAGE
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Human-readable Redfish log message.
              - name: REDFISH_HOST_NAME
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Associated Redfish host name when known.
              - name: REDFISH_SEVERITY
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Source severity.
              - name: REDFISH_MESSAGE_ID
                type: string
                unit: ""
                description: Source registry MessageId.
              - name: REDFISH_JSON
                type: object
                unit: ""
                description: Complete losslessly normalized LogEntry JSON.
          performance: |
            Uses the existing journal SDK and retained backend indexes. The Function performs no Redfish requests.
          security: |
            Retains and exposes complete source LogEntry content, including audit usernames, origin addresses, OEM fields,
            diagnostic data, and message arguments. Linked diagnostic payloads are not dereferenced. Redfish credentials,
            sessions, cookies, client keys, and proxy authorization are never stored.
          availability: Available only while at least one configured `redfish_logs` backend is ready and queryable.
          require_cloud: true
    metrics:
      folding:
        title: Metrics
        enabled: false
      description: |
        The closed executable registry emits standard Redfish contexts only when the endpoint exposes their source properties.
        The `redfish.*` namespace covers endpoint operations, resources, readings, and one-level rollups. Common hardware readings
        reuse `system.hw.sensor.*` contexts with `_collect_module=redfish`.
      availability: []
      dynamic_context_prefixes:
        - prefix: redfish.
          reason: The closed Redfish standard registry materializes optional resource, reading, and one-level rollup contexts by endpoint capability.
        - prefix: system.hw.sensor.
          reason: Standard Redfish temperature, voltage, fan, current, power, energy, humidity, and pressure readings reuse common hardware-sensor contexts.
      scopes:
        - name: endpoint
          description: Per Redfish endpoint job collection and log-routing state.
          labels:
            - name: endpoint_job
              description: Redfish job name.
            - name: endpoint_key
              description: Stable canonical endpoint key.
          metrics:
            - name: redfish.collection.status
              description: Overall endpoint collection result.
              unit: state
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: success
                - name: partial
                - name: unavailable
            - name: redfish.collection.duration
              description: Endpoint collection-cycle duration.
              unit: seconds
              chart_type: line
              dimensions:
                - name: duration
            - name: redfish.collection.http_requests
              description: HTTP request attempts, retries, and redirects in the cycle.
              unit: requests/cycle
              chart_type: line
              dimensions:
                - name: started
                - name: retried
                - name: redirected
            - name: redfish.collection.resources
              description: Resource discovery and acquisition population.
              unit: resources
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: discovered
                - name: readable
                - name: unreadable
                - name: unknown
            - name: redfish.collection.logs_route
              description: Selected log backend route state.
              unit: state
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: disabled
                - name: ready
                - name: unavailable
        - name: resource or reading
          description: Per-component standard resource and normalized-reading charts, optionally attributed to generated ComputerSystem vnodes.
          labels:
            - name: resource_kind
              description: Normalized Redfish resource kind.
            - name: resource_name
              description: Current resource display name.
            - name: logical_owner_name
              description: Proven logical owner name.
            - name: component_family
              description: Cardinality and rollup component family.
          metrics:
            - name: redfish.system.health
              description: ComputerSystem health state.
              unit: state
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: ok
                - name: warning
                - name: critical
                - name: unknown
        - name: one-level rollup
          description: |
            Complete child population aggregated only to its immediate approved rollup owner. The metrics below document the
            invariant and representative rollup shapes; additional `redfish.aggregate.*` summaries, fixed histograms, and state
            counts appear when the endpoint exposes their source capabilities.
          labels:
            - name: rollup_owner_kind
              description: Immediate rollup owner resource kind.
            - name: rollup_owner_name
              description: Current rollup owner display name.
            - name: component_family
              description: Aggregated component family.
          metrics:
            - name: redfish.aggregate.population
              description: Child population and acquisition coverage.
              unit: components
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: total
                - name: readable
                - name: unreadable
                - name: unknown
                - name: histogram_eligible
                - name: histogram_ineligible
            - name: redfish.aggregate.completeness
              description: Collection and histogram completeness state.
              unit: state
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: complete
                - name: incomplete
                - name: histogram_available
                - name: histogram_unavailable
            - name: redfish.aggregate.acquisition_state
              description: Child counts by acquisition state.
              unit: components
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: readable
                - name: unreadable
                - name: unknown
            - name: redfish.aggregate.temperature
              description: Minimum, average, and maximum temperature across the immediate child population.
              unit: Celsius
              chart_type: line
              dimensions:
                - name: minimum
                - name: average
                - name: maximum
            - name: redfish.aggregate.temperature_distribution
              description: Fixed temperature histogram across the immediate child population.
              unit: components
              chart_type: heatmap
              dimensions:
                - name: lt_40
                - name: "40_50"
                - name: "50_60"
                - name: "60_70"
                - name: "70_80"
                - name: "80_85"
                - name: "85_90"
                - name: "90_95"
                - name: "95_100"
                - name: ge_100
            - name: redfish.aggregate.health
              description: Child counts by normalized health state.
              unit: components
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: ok
                - name: warning
                - name: critical
                - name: unknown
            - name: redfish.aggregate.reading_alarm
              description: Child reading counts by normalized alarm state.
              unit: components
              chart_type: stacked
              dimensions:
                - name: clear
                - name: warning
                - name: cap
                - name: alarm
                - name: critical
                - name: emergency
                - name: fault
